{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And the one who sprinkles the waters of impurity.</b> Our Rabbis said that the one who sprinkles is clean, and this comes to teach that the one who carries the waters of sin-offering becomes impure with severe impurity, defiling the garments upon him — which is not so for the one who touches. And his use of the term \"מַזֶּה\" is to tell you that they do not impart impurity until there is in them the measure of sprinkling (Niddah 9)." "<b>And the one who touches — he becomes impure.</b> And does not require washing of garments."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:39.272850843Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}